  "instructions": [
    "Season the cod fillets with a pinch of flaky sea salt and granulated sugar.",
    "Dust the salt block with strong white flour to prevent sticking.",
    "Place the cod fillets on the salt block and sear for 2 minutes on each side.",
    "Transfer the cod to a plate and top with unsalted butter, fresh parsley, and fresh dill.",
    "Drizzle lemon juice and olive oil over the cod to finish.",
    "Place the salt block under the broiler for 30 seconds to create the molten effect.",
    "Remove the salt block from the oven and carefully place the cod on top.",
    "Serve immediately and garnish with additional parsley and dill if desired.",
    "Repeat the process for additional servings.",
    "Note: The salt block should be preheated to 200°C (400°F) before searing the cod."
  ],
